      "cause": "asyncio.timeout cancels AsyncCodex.__aenter__ while SDK awaits asyncio.to_thread(sync.start); the physical startup thread continues. Immediate close can see _proc=None and return success before Popen later returns. The client is neither current nor retired after the timeout, so later close cannot own the process.",
      "evidence": "Real installed AsyncCodex, AsyncCodexClient, CodexClient with only Popen and reader startup replaced by local inert stubs. After timeout and adapter.close SUCCESS, releasing Popen allows _proc assignment; synthetic process is alive and unowned. 1 FAIL, no real process.",
      "fix_boundary": "Keep initialization as an owned shielded operation. A cancelled waiter is not proof the physical startup drained. Bound waiter time, retain/quarantine pending initialization and schedule mandatory cleanup after its terminal result; prevent new generation during unknown cleanup."
    }
  ],
